+# EXEC0153 — source-executed PRG-RAM country write watch (1.53.0-dev1)
+
+This is a genuine linked C11 instrumentation increment to the inherited complete native Genghis Khan I app. It instruments **successful 6502 source-executed writes** to $6000-$7FFF PRG RAM in the existing fail-closed ROM interpreter, distinguishing them from the raw unaligned candidate byte inventory of EXEC0152. The source-country records begin at CPU $6DCD and contain 14×83 and 27×83 bytes respectively. Exclusion upper bounds are $7257 and $768E. All speculative/failed and non-country writes are excluded. First/last PC and country index are recorded only in process-memory result, not published ROM data.
+
+The optional original-ROM command `gk1_native_shell --source-country-write-watch PRIVATE_STOCK_ROM` is **VERIFIED_STATIC source-hypothesis only**, using an explicitly unverified even-pre-render timing model at origin zero. A zero count proves only that no successful country PRG-RAM writes were reached on **that** bounded trace, not that original Spring has no writes. The normal game remains locked at authentic PRE_SETUP without genuine initialization. No player turn, country value, merchant, RNG seed, sound, AI, diplomacy, post-war event, or original first Spring is fabricated.
+
+`test_gk153_country_write_watch` exercises all 83-byte boundary edges including the last two bytes of World country27, first/last source-PC receipt, overflow no-mutation, out-of-range no-mutation, setup guard, invalid ROM atomic rollback and optional exact private original stock source execution. Reproduce via CMake and CTest with optional `GK1_ORIGINAL_STOCK_ROM=/private/stock.nes`; never include stock ROM, source SRAM, screenshots or sound in public GitHub or installer.
+
+Evidence classes: VERIFIED_STATIC traced CPU source under assumptions; inherited OBSERVED_RUNTIME_STOCK fresh and archived independent; TESTED_PORT_LINUX only when binaries/tests actually pass; Win32/NSIS/physical Xbox/full campaigns NOT RUN. This does not close original Spring or constitute a playable release.
